# Portainer safety

## Read-only default

List endpoints, stacks, and containers are fine when Portainer work is
authorized. Do **not**:

- deploy/update/delete a stack
- stop/kill/remove a container
- prune volumes/images that drop data
- change endpoint credentials or access control

…unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn naming the object.

Prefer stopping a named service over whole-stack teardown. Never paste API
tokens or env secrets into chat. Pair volume-wipe risk with compose safety
discipline.
